    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "\ud83e\udda0 Category A: Command & Control (C2)",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "transparent": false,
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "**What is C2 Beaconing?**\nWhen a device gets infected with malware, it 'phones home' to the hacker's server (the Command & Control server) to ask for instructions. This looks like a steady, rhythmic heartbeat of network traffic.\n\n*If you see high numbers here, a device is likely fully infected and waiting for orders.*"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "C2 Beacons Detected",
      "description": "Number of suspected rhythmic beaconing connections detected.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 0
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${PROMETHEUS_DS}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "home_ids_beaconing_c2_count{hostname=~\"$device\"}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "single",
          "sort": "none"
        },
