    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "\ud83d\udce4 Category B: Data Exfiltration",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6
      },
      "transparent": false,
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "**What is Data Exfiltration?**\nHackers try to steal your passwords or files. Sometimes they sneak it out through massive uploads, and sometimes they chop the files into tiny pieces and hide them inside DNS requests (DNS Tunneling).\n\n*If you see huge outbound bytes or long DNS labels, your data might be leaving the network!*"
      }
    },
